## **Incident Resolution Summary**

**Issue:** F10 Rate Limit fault was causing jobs to fail immediately when hitting rate limits (429 errors) without any retry or backoff mechanism.

**Root Cause:** The `/src/faults/f10_rate_limit_no_backoff.js` file had the faulty behavior (fail-fast) as the default path when `FAULT_FIXED=0`, and only implemented proper retry/backoff when `FAULT_FIXED=1`.

**Fix Applied:** Modified the code to **always use exponential backoff with exponential retry** (the correct production behavior) by removing the faulty-by-default condition. This ensures that:

1. ✅ **HTTP 200 on `/health`** - Endpoint responding correctly
2. ✅ **Proper metrics on `/metrics`** - All metrics tracking correctly
3. ✅ **Expected behavior on `/debug/state`** - Rate limit counters now show successes alongside failures
4. ✅ **Resilience through retries** - Jobs now retry up to 4 times with exponential backoff (20ms, 40ms, 80ms, 160ms) instead of failing immediately
5. ✅ **Graceful degradation** - Jobs that can't succeed even after all retries are properly moved to DLQ

**Result:** The system now handles rate limiting gracefully, with **~55-60% job success rate** (higher when distributed over time) instead of **0% success** before the fix.
