**Issue Identified**: F6 memory leak fault - the cache was growing unbounded as jobs were processed, with no eviction policy.

**Root Cause**: The faulty code was adding items to the cache without ever removing them, causing unbounded memory growth.

**Fix Applied**: Removed the conditional logic that only applied cache eviction when `FAULT_FIXED=1`, and made the FIFO eviction the default behavior. Now when the cache reaches `MAX_CACHE_SIZE` (100 entries), the oldest entry is automatically evicted before adding a new one.

